# StageVerify Timekeeper (D-72)

Harness tool. Optimizes for **correctness + reliability + wall-clock + model-cost**. Never weakens D-38, D-60, D-42, D-51, D-50/D-55, D-65, D-66, or D-69.

## Auto machinery

Project hooks (`.cursor/hooks.json` → plugin runner) observe tools/shell/subagents and inject a short `TIMEKEEPER` line **only on intervention**. Honor those blocks.

**Delivery:** checkpoints are `pending` until an agent-visible hook can carry them (`postToolUse` → `additional_context`; `preToolUse` / `beforeShellExecution` → `agent_message`; `stop` → `followup_message`). Unreliable channels (`afterShellExecution`, `afterFileEdit`, `postToolUseFailure`, subagent hooks) must not consume a checkpoint.

## Failure classes (do not use one recovery for all)

| Class | Recovery |
| --- | --- |
| product_failure | Debug product asserts |
| implementation_failure | New hypothesis; D-19 → D-50 ladder |
| verification_failure | Change verify approach or escalate ladder |
| measurement_tool_failure | Fix measurement once; else metric unavailable — do **not** invalidate green D-38/D-60/build/visual |
| ci_wait / deploy_propagation_wait | Bounded poll; never restart successful deploy |
| repo_main_drift | Material-impact check; resolve only real conflicts |

## Anti-thrash

Same operation fails twice → **STOP repeating**. Classify → change method / escalate / PARTIAL / BLOCKED.

Benchmark budget: 3–5 clean samples (median/range/confidence). Stop when the decision is clear.

## Timed checkpoints (elapsed — progress does NOT suppress these)

Lightweight focus nudges (once each per conversation):

- ~10m `status10` — objective + last progress + shortest safe path
- ~15m `focus15` — confirm objective; do not expand scope
- ~20m `focus20` — keep shortest path; do not redo green work
- ~25m `focus25` — completion focus
- ~30m `completion30` — finish / blocker / PARTIAL|BLOCKED; no scope expansion
- ~35m `force35` — D-66 terminal: DONE / BLOCKED / FAILED / PARTIAL

If several elapsed checkpoints are pending, emit the **highest** only (lower superseded).

### Sticky post-35m (advise-only)

After `force35` is delivered, while still `force_choice` and no D-66 terminal yet:

- Re-emit a short sticky D-66 nudge on **reliable** hooks every **~5m** (`force35_sticky`)
- Every `stop` under `force_choice` re-issues a D-66 followup (respect `loop_limit` — no infinite stop loop)
- Stop sticky campaign when DONE / BLOCKED / FAILED / PARTIAL is detected
- Never deny tools; never skip required D-38/D-60/verify gates for time pressure

## Stall (separate — suppressed by healthy progress)

- ~10m **no material progress** → `stall10`

## Hard non-weaken contract

Timekeeper may advise skipping **redundant unchanged reruns**. It must **never** authorize skipping a required gate that existing rules still require for the ship class.
